{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# The Clever Fox\n\nThe old fox had seen many winters pass. Her russet fur, now streaked with silver, told stories of survival in the harsh forest. One autumn evening, she discovered a farmer's henhouse, but instead of attacking, she studied it carefully. The farmer was clever too, and had laid traps everywhere.\n\nShe watched for days, learning his patterns. On the seventh night, when the moon hid behind clouds, she moved. Using a branch to trigger the outer snares harmlessly, she slipped through an overlooked gap in the fence. One hen—that was all she took.\n\nThe farmer found his trap untouched, bewildered. The fox retreated to her den, her belly full, her wit sharper than any tooth. Survival, she knew, belonged to the thoughtful."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002","uuid":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000093"}
